# Reviewed content

Read `docs/operations/authoring.md` before authoring or promoting records. It owns
the public/private boundary, metadata fields, stable permalinks, reviewed assets,
references and LinkedIn semantics.

`site.ts` retains reviewed identity, career and client contributions. Original
reader bodies live in `articles/*.md` or trusted local MDX; `showcase.ts` holds
curated summaries/metadata. `publicationData.ts` adapts them into one eligible
projection. `routes.ts` preserves legacy identities/metadata; `routePages.ts`
retains experience and incumbent-note compatibility.

Public eligibility is separate from work/research maturity. All three new project
areas are In progress, with no supplied demo/repository links. Keep summaries honest;
review substantive Problem, Your role, Architecture, Challenges, Outcome,
Technology and Links material before creating detail pages. Principal/architect
remain goals. Retired student items stay retired.

Keep first-person claims direct and bounded. Named clients have genericised systems;
new metrics, proprietary designs, outcomes or ownership need real review. Preserve
evidence labels and official context as distinct from personal contribution.

Only reviewed public source belongs in committed content. A draft/review/private
metadata label does not conceal a committed file; private drafts stay in ignored
local authoring. Curated LinkedIn is reviewed metadata plus an explicit external
reading destination, with no imported body, local mirror or automatic provider call.
